1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,903
Start by adding your spreadsheets.

2
00:00:02,563 --> 00:00:04,383
You can paste a Google Sheet link, or upload

3
00:00:04,383 --> 00:00:05,203
an Excel file.

4
00:00:06,023 --> 00:00:07,923
Here, we're adding one sheet for St.

5
00:00:08,143 --> 00:00:10,343
Regis, and another for Burj Khalifa.

6
00:00:11,363 --> 00:00:13,503
Each one contains the sellers for that building.

7
00:00:14,343 --> 00:00:17,263
Once they're imported, open Sellers to see everyone together.

8
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:19,995
This is where you can see everyone in one

9
00:00:19,995 --> 00:00:23,615
place: their details, their building, and where things stand.

10
00:00:24,115 --> 00:00:28,075
Filter by prospects, appraisals, for sale, or not interested.

11
00:00:29,215 --> 00:00:31,395
Sold today flags a fresh transaction in that building.

12
00:00:31,815 --> 00:00:33,395
Open a seller and you can see what sold,

13
00:00:33,795 --> 00:00:35,115
when it sold, and for how much.

14
00:00:35,955 --> 00:00:38,815
With WhatsApp connected, those transactions can feed into automated

15
00:00:38,815 --> 00:00:41,475
follow-ups, giving you something useful to share with your

16
00:00:41,475 --> 00:00:41,695
sellers.

17
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,741
You can use the default message, or make it

18
00:00:45,741 --> 00:00:47,181
sound more like you.

19
00:00:48,501 --> 00:00:51,081
In Message templates, write your own wording and drop

20
00:00:51,081 --> 00:00:53,861
in the seller's name, their building, and the latest

21
00:00:53,861 --> 00:00:54,301
transactions.

22
00:00:55,641 --> 00:00:57,861
The preview fills those details in as you go,

23
00:00:58,561 --> 00:01:00,521
so you can see exactly what the message will

24
00:01:00,521 --> 00:01:01,781
look like before you save it.

25
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:07,688
You also decide when those follow-ups go out.

26
00:01:08,108 --> 00:01:10,128
Schedule lets you spread your buildings across the week,

27
00:01:10,488 --> 00:01:12,008
so you can organise them around the way you

28
00:01:12,008 --> 00:01:12,208
work.

29
00:01:18,088 --> 00:01:20,028
Here, we've added buildings from Monday through Thursday.

30
00:01:20,648 --> 00:01:22,948
Save the plan, and the weekly schedule controls which

31
00:01:22,948 --> 00:01:24,708
buildings get follow-ups each day.

32
00:01:25,588 --> 00:01:26,568
Days left empty stay off.

33
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:31,750
Over in Listings, you can track the buildings you

34
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:33,950
cover and spot apartments that have dropped in price.

35
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:36,910
Open a building, then an apartment, to get a

36
00:01:36,910 --> 00:01:37,670
closer look.

37
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:40,450
You can follow the asking price on the chart,

38
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:42,350
and check Activity to see when it changed.

39
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:44,910
It's a useful bit of context before your next

40
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:45,450
conversation.

41
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:50,890
Connect Gmail or Outlook to read emails and draft

42
00:01:50,890 --> 00:01:53,090
replies, with each send confirmed by you.

43
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:55,650
Your calendar brings in upcoming events.

44
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:58,770
And through MCP, you can work with your Repeat

45
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:02,710
AI account from Codex, Claude or ChatGPT.

46
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:06,690
Ask for a seller, check recent WhatsApp messages, or

47
00:02:06,690 --> 00:02:09,050
update a lead, with changes sent to you for

48
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:09,350
approval.

49
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:11,770
So you can keep working in the assistant you

50
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:12,350
already use.

51
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,141
For a quicker way to get things done, there's

52
00:02:16,141 --> 00:02:17,281
Ask Repeat in the corner.

53
00:02:18,261 --> 00:02:20,141
Type what you need, or talk to it using

54
00:02:20,141 --> 00:02:20,481
voice.

55
00:02:21,181 --> 00:02:24,381
It can find sellers, summarise market activity, and help

56
00:02:24,381 --> 00:02:26,101
with things like templates and scheduling.

57
00:02:27,321 --> 00:02:29,881
Here, it's prepared a new message template.

58
00:02:30,241 --> 00:02:31,901
You can read it through and confirm the change

59
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:32,841
when you're happy with it.

60
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:39,018
Repeat AI is available on the web, Windows and

61
00:02:39,018 --> 00:02:40,418
mobile, so you can pick up where you left

62
00:02:40,418 --> 00:02:40,678
off.
